-- the served source (lib/host.cub, h-sync; 2026-11-17, Avik: "There is no canonical state"): the
-- server's pool grows by union with each session's and is never written over. A session asks for the
-- view's entries the server holds after the last it took (STORE/source-log orders them as this server
-- first held them, STORE/logged/ID marks one ordered), takes any object by its hash and kind (text,
-- module, entry), and sends any the server lacks, taken only when its hash is its content's (the
-- machine's --put). Who may send: s-allowed
s-changes-from : Word → Word → List (List Word) → List Word
s-changes-from since i nil = nil
s-changes-from since i (cons l r) = list-append (if wlt since i then h-line (list-append (h-decimal i) (list-append " " l)) else nil) (s-changes-from since (wadd i #1) r)
